---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Clipping Guide for Agents & Developers"
  description="Read Clipping Guide through a public JSON index, Markdown guides, RSS, and sitemap. Source-attributed, dated content with no authentication required."
>
  <div class="wrap page-intro">
    <h1>
      Readable by people.
      <br />
      Accessible to agents.
    </h1>
    <p>The same public guides, in formats that are easy to retrieve and cite.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap plain-page prose">
    <div class="agent-links">
      <a href="/api/guides.json">JSON guide index</a>
      <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt content map</a>
      <a href="/llms-full.txt">Complete guides as text</a>
      <a href="/rss.xml">RSS updates</a>
    </div>
    <h2>How to retrieve a guide</h2>
    <p>
      Use <code>/api/guides.json</code> to discover titles, summaries, topics, publication dates,
      updated dates, sources, canonical URLs, and Markdown URLs. Each guide is available at{' '}
      <code>/guides/&#123;slug&#125;.md</code> and as a normal HTML page.
    </p>
    <h2>Citation & freshness</h2>
    <p>
      Cite the guide's canonical HTML URL and check its updated date. For a platform's rules or
      product features, follow the linked official sources. Research-based comparisons should not be
      presented as independent hands-on tests.
    </p>
    <h2>Public access</h2>
    <p>
      Guide retrieval needs no API key, login, or JavaScript. The <code>llms.txt</code> map is a
      convenience for discovery, not a claim of preferential treatment in search or AI answers.
    </p>
    <h2>Responsible reuse</h2>
    <p>
      Link to the original guide when citing an answer. Preserve caveats, source attribution, and
      example labels. Please do not publish our entire guide collection as another website.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
